{"id": "FC1-c016", "lesson": "L01", "front": "Is the deposit multiplier 1/ρ at every stage?", "back": "No. Under Assumption 2.0 with d > 0 and 0 < ρ ≤ 1, at stage n it is (1 − (1 − ρ)^(n+1))/ρ, which is smaller than 1/ρ at every finite n when ρ < 1 (Proposition 3.1; misconception 2).", "grade": "T"}
{"id": "FC1-c050", "lesson": "L03", "front": "Under B1 to B4, why does the symmetric profile (c+k, c+k) with k ≥ 3 fail to be an equilibrium?", "back": "A dealer undercuts by one cent, to c+k−1, and wins all N shares, earning (k−1)N. At the tie it earns kN/2, and (k−1)N is strictly larger exactly when k > 2 (Proposition 3.2).", "grade": "T"}
{"id": "FC1-c103", "lesson": "L01", "front": "Under Assumption 2.0, do cumulative reserves plus cumulative loans equal total deposits after stages 0 to n?", "back": "Yes. Summing the stage identity over stages 0 to n, the sum of the X_t plus the sum of the ℓ_t equals S_n (Proposition 2.2; Lab 1, Part B prints True).", "grade": "T"}
{"id": "FC1-c105", "lesson": "L03", "front": "What does Assumption A2 of the dealer model fix?", "back": "The dealer has no fees, no interest on cash, no inventory cost and no information. Its cash and its shares are the only two quantities (Assumption A2)."}
{"id": "FC1-c153", "lesson": "L01", "front": "Under leakage (A2′), when does the limit of total deposits equal d/ρ?", "back": "Under A2′ with d > 0, A1 with 0 < ρ ≤ 1, and the no-withdrawal and no-repayment parts of A3, exactly when φ = 1 or ρ = 1 (Proposition 3.5).", "grade": "T"}
